, but }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
dm_draw_objs()}{\loch
 in libdm already renders from }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bview::gv_objs}{\loch
 (or, when }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
v->bsg_root}{\loch
 is set, from }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_root->children}{\loch
 synced from }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
gv_objs}{\loch
). }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
Nothing in the render path actually consumes the }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
gd_headDisplay}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
 chain anymore.}{\loch
 It is now a parallel bookkeeping shadow whose only purpose is to provide the path/grouping/iteration semantics that several features (draw, erase, who, illuminate, redraw, mater color refresh, vdraw, plot, pseudo-solid overlay, name_hash, autoview) still consume. That shadow-tree is the migration crutch the user is asking us to remove.}
