Only the render path uses it}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx3076\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx7193\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx9972\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\loch
Per-node identity (not path-strings)}\cell\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bv_scene_obj *}{\loch
 with }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
s_name}\cell\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\loch
Already universal}\cell\row\pard\trowd\trql\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx3076\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx7193\clpadfl3\clpadl28\clpadft3\clpadt28\clpadfb3\clpadb28\clpadfr3\clpadr28\clvertalc\cellx9972\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\loch
Scene root per view}\cell\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bview::bsg_root}\cell\pard\plain \s24\noline\intbl\ql\noline\ltrpar{\loch
Synced from gv_objs at draw time}\cell\row\pard\pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
So the libbsg substrate to land on is already there. The problem is that }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
none of the features currently driving "what gets drawn" produce or manipulate a BSG tree}{\loch
 \u8212\'97 they all manipulate the legacy display list and rely on a sync shim to mirror the result.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af8\dbch\af10\afs36\ab\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\loch\f3\fs36\b\ql\ltrpar{\loch
3. Cleanup proposal}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
The proposal is in three layers, each independently buildable and testable on top of the previous one:}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af8\dbch\af10\afs28\ab\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\sb140\sa120\keepn\loch\f3\fs28\b\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Layer A \u8212\'97 Reframe the data model so the "drawn set" is a BSG group tree}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
Goal: get rid of }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
struct ged_scene_group}{\loch
 entirely, both as a type and as a concept. The drawn set becomes "the children of a top-level BSG group node owned by the GED instance".}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
A1. Replace }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
gedp->i->ged_gdp->gd_headDisplay}{\loch
 (a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bu_list}{\loch
 of }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
ged_scene_group}{\loch
) with a single per-GED root group node (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_GROUP}{\loch
) plus per-top-level-path subgroups (also }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_GROUP}{\loch
). Each subgroup owns an ordered ptbl of }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_SHAPE}{\loch
 children, not a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bu_list}{\loch
 of }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bv_scene_obj}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
A2. The "drawn name" of a top-level subgroup becomes the group node's }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
s_name}{\loch
 (a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bu_vls}{\loch
). Path semantics are restored by walking the tree (parent group has the prefix; child shape supplies the leaf), not by storing redundant path strings on the group. This kills }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
sg_path}{\loch
 entirely.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
A3. The }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bview::bsg_root}{\loch
 shim's job changes: instead of being re-synced from }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
gv_objs}{\loch
 every frame, the GED-owned group tree IS the canonical structure. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
gv_objs}{\loch
 ptbls become a derived flat index for fast type-bucket queries (DB vs view-only, shared vs local) \u8212\'97 they become a lookup acceleration, not the authoritative store.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
A4. The legacy }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BU_LIST}{\loch
 cross-list "next/prev solid wrap" navigation (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_view_obj_next_solid}{\loch
/}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
prev_solid}{\loch
) is replaced with a depth-first visitor that yields shapes in order. MGED's "advance illuminated solid" then becomes an index into a snapshotted DFS sequence, not a linked-list pointer chase.}
\par \pard\plain \s3\dbch\af8\dbch\af10\afs28\ab\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\sb140\sa120\keepn\loch\f3\fs28\b\ql\ltrpar{\loch
Layer B \u8212\'97 Replace each "feature implemented on the display-list" with a BSG-native implementation}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
The 9 functional roles that }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_view_obj.h}{\loch
 exposes today should be re-expressed as BSG operations:}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
B1. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
Adding a drawn path}{\loch
 (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
lookup_or_add_path}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
append_to_last_group}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
append_solid_to_group}{\loch
): Replace with a "draw context" pattern. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
ged draw foo/bar}{\loch
 becomes "create a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_GROUP}{\loch
 named }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
foo/bar}{\loch
 under the GED root, then for every leaf produced by }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
db_walk_tree}{\loch
 create a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_SHAPE}{\loch
 and attach it as child of that group via }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_group_add_child}{\loch
". }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
dgcdp.gdlp}{\loch
 becomes a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_node *}{\loch
 group. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
dl_redraw}{\loch
 becomes a depth-first re-evaluate of the subtree's shapes, no path-string lookup needed.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
B2. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
Erasing}{\loch
 (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase_by_path}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase_by_name}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase_all_paths}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
headsolid_split*}{\loch
, }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
_dl_eraseFirstSubpath}{\loch
): The "split a group along a subpath" code is the gnarliest legacy code in the file. It only exists because top-level groups are keyed by a path string, so erasing }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
all/foo/bar}{\loch
 from a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
all}{\loch
 group requires materializing }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
all/foo}{\loch
 as a separate sibling. In a true BSG tree, every directory component is already a group node: erasing }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
all/foo/bar}{\loch
 is just "find the subgroup named }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
foo/bar}{\loch
 (or }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bar}{\loch
 under }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
foo}{\loch
) and detach it from its parent via }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_group_remove_child}{\loch
." }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
headsolid_split}{\loch
 and }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
_dl_eraseFirstSubpath}{\loch
 disappear. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
skip_first}{\loch
 semantics (the ad-hoc "the first path component is special" knob from MGED) collapse into ordinary tree-prefix matching with the GED root as the explicit root.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
B3. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
Bounds}{\loch
 (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
bsg_view_obj_bounds}{\loch
): becomes a recursive bbox-fold visitor, or \u8212\'97 better \u8212\'97 caches a node-level bbox that is invalidated by a }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_NODE_SENSOR}{\loch
 when child geometry changes. The }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
pflag}{\loch
 knob ("include phony pseudo-solids?") becomes a flag on the shape node (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
BSG_PAYLOAD_OVERLAY}{\loch
 already exists for this) instead of a runtime check against }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
RT_DIR_PHONY_ADDR}{\loch
.}
\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
B4. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
Color refresh from mater table}{\loch
 (}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
