\par \pard\plain \s20\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa140\sl276\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa140\ltrpar{\loch
R2. }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase}{\rtlch \ltrch\cs16\ab\b\loch
 path-prefix semantics are reformalized in tree terms}{\loch
. Today }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase all/foo/bar}{\loch
 against a draw-set that contains only }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
all}{\loch
 performs a non-obvious "split the group" operation. After B2 the behavior becomes: }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase}{\loch
 operates only at group boundaries \u8212\'97 to erase a sub-component, the parent group must first be expanded (promoted to per-immediate-child subgroups). This is exposed as either an explicit }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
expand}{\loch
 command or implicitly via the existing }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
erase}{\loch
 path-handling: the implementation is cleaner and the observable behavior is unchanged for fully-qualified paths. The }{\rtlch \ltrch\cs15\dbch\af9\dbch\af5\loch\f5\loch
skip_first}{\loch
 knob disappears from the public API (it was always an MGED-internal artefact of how the GED root was implicit).}
\par \pard\plain \s2\dbch\af8\dbch\af10\afs36\ab\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\sb200\sa120\keepn\loch\f3\fs36\b\ql\ltrpar{\loch
5. Phasing & test strategy}
